=== Redistribution analysis ===

Of the 17,820,378 votes cast for eliminated candidates:

{| class="wikitable" style="text-align:right"
|-
! Destination !! Votes !! % of eliminated
|-
| Redistributed to Brito || 11,410,574 || 64.0%
|-
| Redistributed to Riera || 3,548,516 || 19.9%
|-
| Exhausted (no further preference) || 2,861,288 || 16.1%
|-
| '''Total''' || '''17,820,378''' || '''100.0%'''
|}

The overwhelming flow of preferences to Brito reflected the anti-authoritarian coalition's disciplined second-preference strategy. All eliminated candidates except Echeverría had endorsed Brito as their second preference, and the redistribution closely followed these recommendations. The 16.1% exhaustion rate—representing voters who ranked only eliminated candidates without expressing a preference for either frontrunner—was consistent with historical patterns in Baliscan instant-runoff elections.

=== Turnout ===

Turnout of 83.09% was lower than the 87.3% recorded in the confederal election six weeks earlier, a pattern consistent with the typical decline in participation between confederal and premiership elections. Analysts attributed the lower turnout to the widespread perception that Brito's victory was inevitable following the confederal election result, which reduced the urgency of voting for some anti-authoritarian supporters.

