=== International significance ===

Brito's election attracted significant international attention, particularly regarding her status as the world's first openly LGBTQ head of government. In [[Kaftia|Kafto]]-[[Illypnia]] and [[Fosia]], where LGBTQ rights remained contested, her election was met with a mixture of skepticism and hostility from conservative political forces.

The election also had significant implications for the [[Camboriú War]] and the [[Socialist Rapprochement]]. Brito's mandate to pursue a negotiated settlement and her opposition to the domestic nuclear program set the stage for the most significant foreign policy realignment in Baliscan history.

=== Legacy ===

The 1977 premiership election is regarded as one of the most consequential in Baliscan history. It represented:

* The definitive popular rejection of the authoritarian tendencies of the Justino era
* The election of the first woman and first openly LGBTQ head of government worldwide
* A mandate for ecological governance and a negotiated end to the Camboriú War
* The beginning of the end for Balisca's nuclear program
* The consolidation of the anti-authoritarian coalition that would govern Balisca for the following decade

Historian [[Marina Pereira]] described the election as "the moment when Balisca chose its character"—rejecting the vanguardist authoritarianism represented by Justino and reaffirming the anti-statist, participatory tradition of the [[Baliscan Revolution]].

